    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Player archetypes\"\n---\n\n\n\n\nSix style archetypes are fitted jointly on both leagues, with each feature measured relative to its own\nleague and season. Sub-types split each archetype further (e.g. *Alpha scorer*, *Floor general* and\n*Shot-making scorer* inside *On-ball creator*).\n\n![Average profile of each archetype (standard deviations from the league-season mean).](figures/step3_archetype_profiles.png)\n\n**Reading the profile:** each row is an archetype and each column a habit, in standard deviations from the\nleague-season average. Red = more than average, blue = less. On-ball creators use the most possessions and assist the\nmost; spot-up 3-and-D wings take corner threes off passes; rim-running bigs live at the rim and on the glass.\n\n## How the mix has shifted, and what champions did first\n\nFor the three archetypes whose share of minutes moved the most, the line is the league's share (three-season average)\nand the dots are each champion's share. A dot above the line means the champion leaned on that archetype more than the\nleague did that season.\n\n\n\n### NBA (2005-06 to 2025-26)\n\n\n```{=html}\n<div>                            <div id=\"e942dcfc-f043-443d-bcbe-f79e0f6b9f6b\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:400px; width:100%;\"></div>            <script type=\"text/javascript\">                                    window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                    if (document.getElementById(\"e942dcfc-f043-443d-bcbe-f79e0f6b9f6b\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"e942dcfc-f043-443d-bcbe-f79e0f6b9f6b\",                        [{\"hovertemplate\":\"Spot-up 3-and-D wing league: %{y:.0%}\\u003cextra\\u003e\\u003c\\u002fextra\\u003e\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"#2a78d6\",\"width\":2.5},\"mode\":\"lines\",\"name\":\"Spot-up 3-and-D wing (league)\",\"x\":[2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025,2026],